# Client Layout Parity

When changing a GUI client under `apps/`, read
`docs/ux/Layout-Responsive-Spec.md` and compare every shipping GUI client.

- Preserve `navigation sidebar -> items list -> item detail` on desktop.
- Keep storage/vault context in the sidebar above categories and folders.
- Keep search/pagination in the items workspace and secret actions in detail.
- Modifier, hover, focus and loading state must not add/remove layout rows or
  resize columns. Prefer style-only feedback; use a reserved slot or overlay
  only when feedback is necessary.
- Use the whole value surface as the copy target and acknowledge copying by
  styling that same surface. Hold-to-reveal is Option/Alt on macOS and Shift on
  Linux/Windows; always clear it on release or focus loss.
- Share semantics, state transitions and geometry through `zann-ui-core` when
  practical; keep toolkit-native widget appearance in each client.
- For layout changes, update the UX spec and state-level tests in the same
  change. Check COSMIC and Apple; implement the
  change in each or document a time-bounded waiver with owner and rationale.
